About WPP Media

WPP is the trusted growth partner for the world’s leading brands. With exceptional talent, trusted data and intelligence, and world-class partnerships - all united by our pioneering agentic marketing platform, WPP Open - we help clients navigate change, capture opportunity, and deliver transformational growth. 

WPP Media is WPP's AI-driven media operating unit, bringing together media, data, and partnerships to deliver creative personalisation at scale. Connected through WPP Open and powered by Open Intelligence, clients see exactly where, how, and why their media investment is working.

For more information, visit wppmedia.com .

&nbsp;Mindshare: A Leading WPP Media Brand

Mindshare delivers Good Growth for its clients. As “Growth Architects," we drive growth that benefits all stakeholders - better for people, planet, and business - by using media with intention. This approach creates more meaningful connections with consumers, increases consumer trust in the brand, and delivers better outcomes for all stakeholders.

Role Summary and Impact

The Senior associate will lead the development and execution of integrated media strategies across digital, TV, print, and out-of-home channels to enhance client presence, drive engagement, and achieve marketing goals, ultimately delivering significant growth and brand awareness for our clients. This role is ideal for a senior media professional with proven experience across multiple media channels, who is ready to lead complex projects, manage client relationships, and contribute to strategic planning at a senior level.&nbsp;

• Develop and implement comprehensive integrated media strategies across TV, radio, print, out-of-home, and digital channels to support marketing objectives and enhance brand visibility.&nbsp;

• Analyze market trends and audience data across all media channels to inform strategy and guide senior-level, data-driven decisions.&nbsp;

• Design, execute, and oversee integrated campaigns across multiple channels, including TV, radio, print, out-of-home, social media, and digital advertising.&nbsp;

• Lead the end-to-end process of integrated media campaigns from concept to execution, including budget management, media buying negotiations, and performance tracking.&nbsp;

• Develop and manage an integrated media plan and calendar that aligns with marketing goals, audience insights, and channel mix.&nbsp;

• Collaborate with internal teams, external partners, and media owners to negotiate rates and create high-quality, high-impact media placements.&nbsp;

• Plan and manage paid media campaigns across traditional and digital channels, including TV, radio, print, OOH, PPC, display ads, and social media ads.&nbsp;

• Track, analyze, and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) across all integrated media activities, presenting findings to senior stakeholders and clients.&nbsp;

• Provide senior-level insights and strategic recommendations based on performance data to improve campaign effectiveness, media efficiency, and ROI.&nbsp;

Skills and Experience

At&nbsp;WPP Media, we believe in the power of our culture and our people. It’s what elevates us to deliver exceptional experiences for both our clients and each other. In this role it will be critical to embrace&nbsp;WPP &amp;&nbsp;WPP Media’s&nbsp;shared&nbsp;core&nbsp;values:

• Be&nbsp;Extraordinary&nbsp;by&nbsp;Leading Collectively&nbsp;to&nbsp;Inspire transformational Creativity.

• Create an&nbsp;Open&nbsp;environment by&nbsp;Balancing People and Client Experiences&nbsp;by&nbsp;Cultivating Trust.

• Lead&nbsp;Optimistically&nbsp;by&nbsp;Championing Growth&nbsp;and Development&nbsp;to&nbsp;Mobilize the Enterprise.

• Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, Media, or a related field.

• Minimum of 4-5 years of experience in integrated media, media planning/buying, or a related senior role.

• Proven experience across traditional and digital media platforms, including TV, radio, print, OOH, a

